  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "During the three-venerable fight over wild rank nine light Gu, Giant Sun Immortal Venerable activates more trump card killer moves, including Poor Luck Silver Hook. Fang Yuan senses the approach and leaves the spot at once with wind-light-fire-lightning wheels.",
      "chapters": [
        2280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A pure silver curved hook appears at the spot Fang Yuan just left, then vanishes after only a moment, so fast it seems like an illusion. The silver hook keeps appearing at the places he moves to, only moments from hitting him.",
      "chapters": [
        2280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan judges that Giant Sun Immortal Venerable has never used this luck path killer move before, and that a hit would make his luck fall greatly. With the retaliation of all three venerables’ luck, he treats contact as a detrimental blow. Star Constellation Immortal Venerable notes that Cooking Luck Pot’s protection could resist the silver hook so he could attack Light Emperor, but he chooses to dodge instead. He does not even want to touch the silver hook while most of his attention is on refining heavenly secret Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        2280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
